  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Taiwanin C may interact with Tankyrase-2 through a series of molecular targets. The compound is implicated in targeting Caspase-5, which is a key enzyme in the apoptosis pathway. Caspase-5 is further targeted by two different compounds, Isotorachrysone-6-O-alpha-D-ribofuranoside and Lethedioside B, both of which also target Tankyrase-2. This indicates a potential pathway where Taiwanin C may exert its effects through Caspase-5, which in turn influences Tankyrase-2. The scores from the three paths are consistent, suggesting a reliable relationship between Taiwanin C and Tankyrase-2. The mechanism appears to involve Caspase-5 as a central mediator, with the compound potentially modulating the activity of Tankyrase-2 through its interaction with these downstream targets. The evidence supports a plausible biological link, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
